  "identity": "For descending giant indices g, maintain A=sum_h Rot((h-g)*k,inner_h). Move from previous p to g via A=Rot((p-g)*k,A)+inner_g. Rotate by the final smallest g*k after the last group. Duplicate indices require no rotation, and gaps remain valid. Each inner group is reconstructed and rounded exactly where it was before; no rounding is moved across a sum.",
